          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21104 ptlrpc: make an idle import valid when activated",
        "message": "LU-21104 ptlrpc: make an idle import valid when activated\n\nDeactivating an import marks it invalid.  For a connected import, the\nreconnect started when it is activated again makes it valid, but an\nimport that was IDLE is not reconnected: ptlrpc_recover_import()->\nptlrpc_set_import_discon() only acts a FULL import, so the idle import\nwill not be able to be recovered, so all I/O to the OST fails:\n\n  client# lctl set_param osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-*.active=0\n  client# lctl set_param osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-*.active=1\n  client# touch /mnt/lustre/f\n  touch: setting times of '/mnt/lustre/f': Input/output error\n\nIn ptlrpc_set_import_active(), mark an idle import valid with\nptlrpc_activate_import() without reconnecting it, so that it connects\non its next request like any other idle import.\n\nFixes: 5a6ceb664f07 (\"LU-7236 ptlrpc: idle connections can disconnect\")\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I99cf02892a690346754e2218f7b2fa9c746e0f8e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
